{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHp5pahTDDiwUZ5jurvH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most of this set goes back: I blessed two of the three amendments and returned all four new rows. The verdict is committed as `94c67640f` in `docs/reviews/wi-960/005-ADJUDICATE-2373372.md`, with both required trailers. Every cited test exists.\n\n**Amendments (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`):**\n- **LLR-269, blessed:** the record operation now commits a log only from a claimed linked worktree. From anywhere else it writes the log to the primary checkout's spool (its holding folder for logs) and commits nothing; if the claim can't be read, it spools. The resume and retained-session refusals are also new. Each clause is observable and matches the code.\n- **TC-265, blessed:** its new arms match LLR-269's clauses one for one.\n- **LLR-270, not blessed:** it contradicts itself. It keeps \"the ping's log is written and committed by the dispatcher's own thread … only over a clean trunk\", then adds that a dispatcher-rooted ping spools and commits nothing. The dispatcher's warmer is always rooted at the primary checkout, and the new test confirms nothing is committed, so the old clause can't describe any ping now. Approved TC-268's Method still says the ping \"commits it\" too, and this lane didn't amend it.\n\n**First approval (`OUTCOME: RETURN rows=4`):**\n- **SR-243:**\n  - There is no perspective record, the same gap WI-957 and WI-958 fixed.\n  - Its acceptance adds the resume-carrier refusal and the whole edit check, which its Requirement never states. An acceptance cell can only measure what the requirement obliges, a point SR-026's rationale already makes.\n- **LLR-346:** it opens with \"A coordinator call shall …\", but `shall` belongs at SR level. It also requires published guidance naming this route as the only Sol or Terra launch path, which SR-243 doesn't ask for. That is the same shape I returned in WI-957.\n- **TC-384:** its Expected omits the edit-judgement outcomes and \"a refused commit is never success\". Its tests check those, but the cell doesn't claim them.\n- **TC-385:** it is sound as written, but it verifies exactly the guidance clause that may move.\n\nOne thing I checked and didn't count as a finding: LLR-346 traces this repo's own coordinator tooling, which approved rows LLR-340 and LLR-301 already do.\n\n**The follow-up draft** in the verdict's `## Dispositions` asks to:\n- write and check the perspective record;\n- bring SR-243's Requirement in line with its acceptance;\n- remove the `shall` and resolve the guidance clause;\n- extend TC-384's Expected;\n- rewrite LLR-270's keep-warm clause and amend TC-268 with it;\n- then re-sit the six rows.\n\nLLR-269's and TC-265's blessings stand. As before, the hook's `format` step was skipped because ruff isn't installed for its Python 3.12, and I left the coordinator's `.requested` marker untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5728,"cache_read_input_tokens":845548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5728},"output_tokens":725,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"d8d266d4-d557-4f3f-b882-fbb4c3e8961a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:16:59.610Z","request_id":"req_011CgHp5owWe4dUJk4BRHY5m"}
